WEBVTT

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:02.430
I found it! Over there!

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:03.960
Hoi! Joso!

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:05.530
Ketsu!

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.960
What were you thinking?!

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:12.140
You'll need extra lives if
you keep fighting like that...

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:15.100
Yoshi, you've got to stay quick
during a challenge!

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.780
Hey, Tokine, are you okay?

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:22.450
High school student Yukimura Tokine and
junior high student Sumimura Yoshimori

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:24.250
are ordinary students by day.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:29.360
But at night, their mission is to
protect the Karasumori Site,

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.550
where the school now stands.
From the Ayakashi.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.220
I will become stronger!

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:39.260
I never want to see her hurt again!

00:00:54.820 --> 00:01:00.090
The dangerous forest invites me
It's showtime again tonight

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:01.960
(Ayakashi NIGHT)

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:07.160
Everyone's rampaging
with all their strength

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.060
(Fighting late into the night)

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:12.500
Drive away all hesitation

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:16.900
Wanna take them on? Yeah

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:20.440
I will protect you
(No matter what)

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:23.780
I will protect you that's all
(that's all I want)

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:29.450
Goodbye to the days
when all I'd do was cry

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:33.950
Sha la la la la...

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:40.360
I hold words in my heart
that I'd like to say

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.330
(Secret romance)

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:47.540
Standing in front of me is someone
I don't want to lose

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.300
(A strange distance)

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:56.140
I can't stand watching
people get hurt anymore

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:57.210
Yeah

00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:00.680
I wanna be your knight
(I wanna be strong)

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:04.290
I wanna be your light
(More than I am now)

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:09.620
Someday I'll share with you
my 100% smile

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.700
Gently now... gently...

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:24.830
I know...

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:28.670
Look! Look at this height!
Look at this luster!

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:31.400
Congrats! You finally finished it!

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:34.540
But I can't be satisfied just yet!

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:37.520
One day, I'm going to build
a castle out of cake that I can live in!

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:39.480
That's one heck of
a dream you've got!

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:41.990
I'll do it someday.

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:44.780
You taught me a lot, you know!

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:46.730
Aren't I useful?

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:48.330
By the way...

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:52.190
Maybe you should pass on soon.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:55.500
It's not good to stay in
this world for too long.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.800
Well, I am thinking about it too.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:00.360
What regrets are keeping you here?

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:04.540
Well... I guess it's probably...

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:05.870
You know, my last words...

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:12.650
C-Cabbage...

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:16.860
A pâtissier going out to buy cabbage

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:20.060
and getting in a motorcycle accident
on the way back is a bit stupid.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:22.690
But you know, I actually like it
the way it is right now.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.020
I went to the hot springs the other day.

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:29.970
Oh... Wait! You're a ghost!
Why did you go to the hot springs?

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.130
You went peeping, didn't you!

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:34.410
The hot spring inns are really nice!

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:38.170
After seeing that, there's nothing better
than living the life of a monster!

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:41.410
Well, see ya, do your best!

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:43.240
Hey!

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.830
Next person, please!

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:58.290
Now I can finally pass on!

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:02.790
Hello...

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:05.230
Oh. Yo-chan! You were here?

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:07.170
I'm sorry you had to wait!

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.410
No, that's all right.

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:13.150
There have been so many ghosts
coming in to see me recently.

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:15.310
I guess this place is getting popular.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:20.690
Well, you're the only person that would
listen to the ghosts' troubles for free.

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:26.690
You don't come in to see me anymore.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:28.890
To top it off, you keep
sending ghosts my way too!

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:30.050
I'm sorry.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:34.230
That's okay!
I do this because I want to.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:36.600
So what is it that you wanted today?

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:39.100
It's about the pâtissier ghost.

00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:42.880
Did he say anything
when he came here?

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:48.580
Nothing, really.
But it's dangerous to leave him be.

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:52.010
He could turn into
something very bad.

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:55.190
I really want to help him pass on!

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:57.560
I knew you would say that.

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:02.860
Then let's go find out
the real reason why he can't pass on.

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:04.560
Y-Yeah...

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:11.090
Where are we going?

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:16.540
According to what he said,
it should be somewhere around here...

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:17.930
Found it!

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:20.510
This is the bakery where he worked!

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.810
The guy who speaks in Kansai dialect?

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:25.720
Oh, you mean Fishcake Boy.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.350
F-Fishcake Boy?!

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.520
You mean him, right?

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:33.290
Yes! Him! There's no mistake!

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:35.790
Would you please tell us about him?

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:36.820
Back when he was still alive.

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:38.800
When he was still alive...

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:42.470
I can't help but think Fishcake Boy
is still alive and well somewhere...

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.960
It was just so sudden...

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:47.800
Excuse me, why is
his nickname Fishcake Boy?

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:51.710
He was the heir to
the Tsukijigaoka Food Corporation.

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:52.470
What?!

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:54.380
You mean that company
that's famous for fishcakes?

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:57.280
Yeah. Couldn't you tell
from his name?

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:59.050
It's Tsukijigaoka Masahiko.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:03.290
That was his name huh
Tsukijigaoka Masahiko...

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:06.330
He should have taken over
his family business,

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:08.330
but he said he wanted to
become a pâtissier,

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:10.030
so he took an apprenticeship
under me.

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:12.930
Was there something that
always bothered him?

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:14.200
Something that he was always
concerned with?

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:17.400
I don't know...
Maybe his little brother?

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:18.660
Little brother?

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:19.960
I wonder why.

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:24.240
Masahiko's parents passed away
when he was still small.

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:25.170
- What?!
- What?!

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:29.380
I heard his uncle that ran
the Tsukijigaoka Food Corporation

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:31.150
adopted him and his brother.

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:36.120
He left his brother behind.
So I'm sure he was very worried.

00:06:36.590 --> 00:06:38.860
Is his brother still with his uncle?

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:43.000
He lives around here now.
But I don't know any more than that.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.960
All right. Thank you very much
for your time.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:51.260
Say, why do you guys want to
know about Fishcake Boy?

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:55.440
We want him to... rest in peace.

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:56.700
What?

00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:58.680
Oh! Take a look at this!

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:02.810
New item, "Cabbage Patch."

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:07.680
That new item is something Masahiko
and I were going to make together.

00:07:08.090 --> 00:07:09.520
It tastes great!

00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:11.580
I put a lot of effort into that.

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:13.460
For his sake too.

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:15.330
So that's what happened...

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:23.100
The reason why he can't pass on
is because of his little brother.

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:24.830
So what should we do?

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:29.010
We will have to
resort to drastic measures!

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:30.570
Excuse me?

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:38.080
What did you say?

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:41.320
I said we're going to go see
your little brother!

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:42.990
No way!

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:45.390
Why?! Don't you want to pass on?

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:46.620
Oh. look at the time.
I got to go now.

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:47.320
See ya.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.760
You don't even have a watch!

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.030
I'm taking you with me even
if I have to tie you up!

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:58.030
Don't be stupid!
You can't tie down a ghost! See ya!

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:03.040
I can't aim very well with it right now,
but it's worth a try.

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:05.670
Nenshi!

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:12.150
What?!

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:19.920
Now, let's go!

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:23.530
Somebody help!
We have a kidnapper here!

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:24.950
Hey!

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:27.130
You're a student!
Shouldn't you be in school?!

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:29.970
Who is Sumimura talking to?

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:35.170
Sorry to say this, but today is Saturday,
so there's no school! Give it up!

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:38.710
According to my data, people like that
should be ignored and left alone.

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:42.210
Yo-chan! Over here!

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:45.740
Sorry I'm late.
He kept refusing to come with me.

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:48.550
Oh my. What's that wonderful thread?

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:51.250
It's called a Nenshi.
And it can bind ghosts too.

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:55.460
How convenient! Anyway, let's tail
behind his little brother!

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:56.420
Tail behind?

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:59.290
I disguised myself just
for that today.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:02.300
Dis... guise?

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:06.570
His little brother's name is
Tsukijigaoka Toshihiko-san.

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:09.570
He took up a post as the branch president
of the Kanto region.

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:11.200
Oh?

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:12.510
He's very diligent, and brilliant,

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:15.240
and they say that he's very close to
becoming the company president.

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:19.020
He seems to be doing fine.
What are you worried about?

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:24.030
Because... I am.
I'm his older brother.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:28.020
Oh? Then why don't you want to see him?

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:32.560
Our plan will be simple.

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:36.400
We'll follow behind the little brother
and wait until he's alone.

00:09:36.670 --> 00:09:38.230
We'll stick close until then, all right?

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:39.230
We're going to do it nonstop?!

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:42.070
I have work to do at night,
so I have to go home later!

00:09:42.280 --> 00:09:44.140
Yeah, I hope you can go home too.

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:48.670
Madam! The target is in sight!

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:50.620
You have good eyes, Ogata.

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:51.840
Yes!

00:09:51.890 --> 00:09:53.980
I have the utmost confidence
in my sight and beautiful face!

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:57.090
Now let's tail him!

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:59.750
Wait... Isn't using this car
going to stand out?

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:06.400
According to the secret information
that Ogata found,

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:08.470
the little brother will be
making his rounds

00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:10.870
to sales offices and factories
for the entire day today.

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:18.710
It doesn't seem like
we'll catch him when he's alone.

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:25.150
You can go back to the office first.
I need to run an errand.

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:26.310
All right.

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:30.080
Madam! He will be alone soon!

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:31.760
Very good! Let's follow him!

00:10:37.730 --> 00:10:39.390
Don't lose him, Ogata!

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:43.300
Yes. Madam! I will utilize
my past experience to the fullest!

00:10:43.840 --> 00:10:47.210
Your past experience?!
What did you used to do?!

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:48.600
Now listen carefully.

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:50.910
You have to tell him
how you feel so you can pass on!

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:53.280
I don't want to do this!
Let me go home!

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:55.780
What are you saying?

00:10:55.950 --> 00:11:01.080
Your soul will never pass on
until you face your brother!

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:02.350
Get that through your head!

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:07.820
But... I feel so ashamed...

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:12.330
He... definitely hates me right now...

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:16.600
I was supposed to
succeed that company...

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:20.370
But I said that I wanted
to become a pâtissier

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:22.240
and forced all those
responsibilities onto him.

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:26.380
He... He never complained
about it even once.

00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:30.480
I took advantage of his honest
and hard-working personality...

00:11:33.350 --> 00:11:36.810
Madam, the target's car has stopped.

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:39.350
What's wrong?

00:11:39.930 --> 00:11:42.590
That place is where I had my accident...

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:49.330
It's all right.

00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:52.470
Your brother doesn't hate you.

00:11:53.110 --> 00:11:56.010
If he did. He wouldn't
come all the way here.

00:11:56.510 --> 00:11:57.170
Let's go!

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:03.240
Excuse me!

00:12:04.020 --> 00:12:07.750
I need to have a word with you.
I'll get straight to the point.

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:12.890
The ghost of your brother, Masahiko-san,
is still wandering and cannot pass on

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:14.420
because he is worried about you.

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:20.930
Mother-san! That's too sudden...

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:22.770
I-I suppose so...

00:12:23.270 --> 00:12:26.140
We actually brought
your brother's ghost with us today.

00:12:29.840 --> 00:12:31.640
What do you people want?!

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:33.550
Did you find out about
my brother's connection with me?

00:12:34.280 --> 00:12:36.650
Is that why you're saying
these idiotic things?

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:38.450
See?! It's impossible!

00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:42.210
Toshihiko is too serious.
He doesn't believe in ghosts!

00:12:42.290 --> 00:12:42.950
Hey!

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:45.390
I'll try to pass on in my own way!

00:12:46.230 --> 00:12:47.630
What are you saying?!

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:49.630
What happened to
your endless optimism?

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:52.020
Stop running away from your brother!

00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:54.330
You don't know my feelings!

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:55.030
I don't care!

00:12:55.070 --> 00:12:58.770
Stop peeping at the hot springs
and face your brother!

00:12:59.470 --> 00:13:00.460
Hot springs?

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:02.740
E-Excuse me...

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:06.080
Would you please listen to us,
just for a bit?

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:09.950
Do you hate your brother?

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:17.720
My brother? Yes. I hate him.

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:24.360
What do you people want?
Is it money?

00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:27.860
Absolutely not! We just want
Masahiko-san to rest in peace!

00:13:30.340 --> 00:13:32.860
I will come back here
tomorrow at four.

00:13:33.980 --> 00:13:36.500
If my brother is really with you,
show me some kind of proof.

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:39.040
I'll listen to what you have
to say then.

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:50.790
We don't have any proof...

00:13:56.030 --> 00:13:59.230
What kind of proof do we need
so that he'll believe us?

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:01.130
It's okay.

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:05.830
He already hates me,
so I can't trouble him anymore.

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:07.360
Oh no, you don't.

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:12.340
At this rate, you might even come
to possess your brother.

00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:14.780
It might happen against your will.

00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:19.680
I also think that you should tell
your brother how you really feel.

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:22.750
I'm sure there's something
you want to tell him.

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:24.420
Yeah...

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:30.260
I really need to apologize to him.

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:32.920
Now that's settled. We have to find out
what to do about the proof.

00:14:33.170 --> 00:14:34.660
Do you have any ideas?

00:14:35.670 --> 00:14:36.660
Let's see...

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:40.540
When I was small.
I baked a cake for him.

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:42.840
Why don't I try that again?

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:44.880
Sounds great! Let's make it!

00:14:45.510 --> 00:14:47.740
I can't bake with these hands anymore...

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:50.340
Don't worry, leave it to me!

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:52.880
Then let's start right away!

00:14:53.190 --> 00:14:55.780
Hold on, I have to work tonight.

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:58.560
Then we'll get things ready and
you can come tomorrow morning.

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:02.350
How does that sound. Yo-chan?

00:15:02.530 --> 00:15:03.190
Gotcha!

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:08.430
Ogata, have you made
the preparations?

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:13.070
Yes, Madam. I brought all
the necessary materials.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:16.380
Now let's start making
that cake from your memories!

00:15:16.610 --> 00:15:17.740
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:22.810
The ingredients you use seem
to be really simple.

00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:24.940
I made it when I was in 4th grade.

00:15:24.990 --> 00:15:27.110
It was the first cake I ever baked.

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:44.390
How's this?

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:46.070
This isn't it.

00:15:46.240 --> 00:15:47.670
What's wrong with it?

00:15:47.910 --> 00:15:49.380
I'm doing it exactly the way
you're telling me!

00:15:50.310 --> 00:15:54.410
It has to be sort of like...
thick and also sluggish!

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:55.610
I don't get it!

00:15:55.950 --> 00:16:00.320
This is bad. We only have
two hours until the deadline.

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:04.590
I guess I can't recreate
what I did 18 years ago.

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:08.300
For that cake, I just tried frantically to
get it close to my mother's cake...

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:09.650
Your mother's?

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:14.930
Yeah. Our mother always baked
cakes for us.

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:18.230
I tried to imitate her for this cake.

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:21.180
After our parents passed away,

00:16:21.180 --> 00:16:24.580
Toshihiko got so depressed
he never even went outside.

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:29.580
That's why I used up my allowance
to buy him a present...

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:32.210
and stared long and hard at the books
while trying to make the cake.

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:37.330
So on his birthday,
I gave both of them to him,

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:41.090
saying they were from
Mom and Dad in heaven.

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:46.390
He had been crying all this time,
but he finally smiled for me.

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:49.000
I was so happy.

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:52.870
I never knew that seeing someone else
smile could make me happy.

00:16:53.710 --> 00:16:55.540
Thinking back, I guess after that,

00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:58.980
I decided to try and bring happiness
to people through sweets.

00:17:00.050 --> 00:17:02.120
Well. Then I left home...

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:05.090
but having him hate me
brings it full circle.

00:17:06.890 --> 00:17:09.080
Let's do this! We have enough
to bake one more cake!

00:17:09.390 --> 00:17:12.380
We need to make
your brother smile again!

00:17:14.730 --> 00:17:15.390
Yeah!

00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:27.030
Floor it, Ogata.

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:28.060
Yes. Madam.

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:31.270
Make sure you don't get caught.

00:17:31.510 --> 00:17:35.920
Yes, Madam! I will prove that
my Class-A license is not only for show!

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:40.350
A Class-A license?
Why does a butler need that?!

00:17:43.590 --> 00:17:44.580
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

00:17:48.800 --> 00:17:50.460
We'll all die if we get into an accident!

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:51.930
You're already dead!

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:10.110
I didn't think
you would actually come.

00:18:10.420 --> 00:18:11.410
Of course we did.

00:18:11.950 --> 00:18:14.680
And this is our proof.
Please take a look.

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:17.990
It is supposed to be
a very memorable cake.

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:22.020
When you were children,
he made this on your birthday-

00:18:22.060 --> 00:18:23.550
It's all messed up!

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:24.590
What?!

00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:27.100
But we really made this
with your brother.

00:18:27.570 --> 00:18:28.870
Would you please try it?

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:30.290
That will be quite all right.

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:31.100
But...

00:18:31.470 --> 00:18:34.570
I'm sorry.
It's because I had them hurry over...

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:37.040
No, it's my fault for
not holding it better.

00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:39.170
I can tell without eating it.

00:18:39.580 --> 00:18:40.240
Huh?

00:18:41.750 --> 00:18:42.840
I believe you.

00:18:43.420 --> 00:18:46.290
The idea of a dead person
baking a cake...

00:18:46.290 --> 00:18:48.190
No mistake, my brother would do that.

00:18:48.720 --> 00:18:53.490
He did the same thing long ago by saying
a cake was baked by our late mother,

00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:54.860
but I didn't think he'd do it again.

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:56.090
Do it again?

00:18:56.130 --> 00:19:00.860
So you knew that cake was
baked by your brother?

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:04.600
I could tell right away that
it wasn't baked by our mother.

00:19:05.570 --> 00:19:08.130
To be honest. That cake looked
much worse than this one.

00:19:08.380 --> 00:19:10.640
What?! Was it that bad?

00:19:11.050 --> 00:19:14.170
But he said that you ate it
and smiled for him.

00:19:14.980 --> 00:19:19.580
Well, it made me very happy.

00:19:20.190 --> 00:19:22.590
He said the present and cake
were from our parents in heaven.

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:27.290
I knew he was making it up,
but he did all that for me...

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:30.360
I thought to myself that I should straighten up
so he wouldn't have to worry about me.

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:34.630
Oh my. You were a very strong person
even when you were little.

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:37.700
I'm not as strong as my brother.

00:19:38.610 --> 00:19:42.130
After our parents passed away,
I did nothing but cry.

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:44.800
But my brother
didn't cry even once.

00:19:45.250 --> 00:19:51.280
Your brother wants to apologize for
making you take over the family business.

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:54.020
H-Hey, Toshihiko...

00:19:54.490 --> 00:19:57.180
I was supposed to be the older brother,
but I was selfish and did my own thing.

00:19:57.830 --> 00:19:58.480
I'm really sorr-

00:19:58.530 --> 00:20:00.990
Why are you apologizing for that?

00:20:01.230 --> 00:20:01.890
- Huh?
- Huh?

00:20:02.230 --> 00:20:04.760
Didn't you say you hated
your brother?

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:10.640
Oh... I hated him for dying
on me so suddenly!

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:14.040
I never thought my brother
would die too!

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:19.180
But you always had
that bored look on your face.

00:20:19.710 --> 00:20:23.880
Your brother is saying that
you always had a bored look on your face.

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:28.650
There is another reason
why I decided to believe you.

00:20:29.090 --> 00:20:30.080
I don't care!

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:33.420
Stop peeping at the hot springs
and face your brother!

00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:36.590
When I went to a hot springs inn
the other day,

00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:39.290
I felt that someone was
watching over me.

00:20:39.930 --> 00:20:42.130
So it was my brother all along.

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:45.700
He even appeared in my dream
and tried to make me laugh.

00:20:46.740 --> 00:20:49.140
I've just been a little tired.

00:20:49.940 --> 00:20:51.780
Did I make him worry
about me again?

00:20:52.150 --> 00:20:55.410
Oh I get it...
He wasn't there just to peep...

00:20:56.420 --> 00:20:58.720
May I have that?

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:00.420
Huh? Oh, go ahead.

00:21:01.120 --> 00:21:02.560
I wonder if I can finish it all.

00:21:05.460 --> 00:21:07.390
Is my brother there?

00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:14.330
Bro! Your cakes are
the best in the world!

00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:17.770
Remembering them
puts a smile on my face!

00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:18.930
It's like a magical cake!

00:21:19.640 --> 00:21:22.110
That's why... as long as I have this...

00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:23.440
I'll be okay.

00:21:24.850 --> 00:21:27.080
You don't need to worry about me.

00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:36.920
Thank you for everything.

00:21:37.860 --> 00:21:38.850
Don't mention it.

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:41.990
I'm so glad I'm a ghost...

00:21:42.660 --> 00:21:45.390
I didn't have to let him see me cry
even at the very end.

00:21:58.450 --> 00:22:01.070
Did my brother just... leave?

00:22:01.550 --> 00:22:02.210
Yes.

00:22:06.990 --> 00:22:07.650
Thank you.

00:22:11.360 --> 00:22:15.590
The test cakes that I baked with him...
were unbelievably bad.

00:22:17.630 --> 00:22:21.070
But one day, I want to
bake a cake like that.

00:22:22.270 --> 00:22:23.260
You're late!

00:22:23.640 --> 00:22:24.630
Shut up!

00:22:25.370 --> 00:22:27.310
A cake that makes people's hearts
and souls happy...

00:22:28.110 --> 00:22:29.300
The best cake in the world!

00:22:38.350 --> 00:22:46.060
The breeze blows past us
in this city we know so well

00:22:46.060 --> 00:22:52.760
The two of us both walk at our usual pace

00:22:54.340 --> 00:23:02.140
Joking around I noticed after I laughed

00:23:02.140 --> 00:23:08.480
Your mature look that
I had never seen before

00:23:10.420 --> 00:23:18.330
You don't have to say anything it's okay

00:23:19.630 --> 00:23:24.690
I'm not mistaking these feelings

00:23:26.270 --> 00:23:33.770
Straight ahead I'm pushing forward

00:23:33.770 --> 00:23:41.310
Yet I can't help but keep gazing at you

00:23:43.050 --> 00:23:50.290
Even if we are near or far

00:23:50.290 --> 00:23:58.860
The red string connects one to another
